# Copy to .env.local for local development, and set the same values in
# Vercel > Settings > Environment Variables for deployments.
#
# All of these are server-only secrets. Never rename them with a NEXT_PUBLIC_
# prefix — anyone holding a key can post as this site.

# ---- Contact form -> Aleesa CRM (Website Form) ----------------------
# Aleesa dashboard > Settings > Connections > Website Form > "Enable Website
# Form". Copy the key there and then — only a masked version is shown later,
# and regenerating it invalidates the old key immediately.
# Unset: enquiries from /contact are only logged server-side.
# ALEESA_WEBSITE_FORM_API_KEY=wform_...
# Optional, defaults to https://api.aleesa.ai. (The dashboard may print
# "api-aleesa.ai", which does not resolve — use the dotted host.)
# ALEESA_API_URL=https://api.aleesa.ai

# ---- Chat widget -> Aleesa Web Chat ---------------------------------
# Aleesa dashboard > Settings > Connections > Web Chat > "Enable Web Chat".
# Set BOTH and the widget is answered by Aleesa (trained in the dashboard's
# Knowledge Base + Chat Agent); conversations land in the Aleesa inbox.
# Unset: the widget answers from the built-in knowledge base in lib/chatbot.
# ALEESA_WEBHOOK_URL is the webhook server origin; "/webhooks/web-chat" is
# appended automatically.
# ALEESA_WEBHOOK_URL=https://webhooks.your-aleesa-host.com
# ALEESA_WEBCHAT_API_KEY=

# ---- Contact form captcha -> Cloudflare Turnstile -------------------
# Cloudflare dashboard > Turnstile > widget. The site key is public (hence
# the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix); the secret key is server-only. The widget's
# Hostname Management must list the live domain.
# Required: without them the form rejects every submission.
# Local dev can use Cloudflare's always-pass test keys:
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
